I looked at Kasper and Sara and smiled.
"I arrived in Denmark in January," I said.
It was a very cold day.
Kasper asked:
"How was the weather?"
"The sky was completely grey," I answered.
I stood outside the airport with my two large bags.
The wind blew, and I was freezing.
Sara drank a little water and nodded.
"January is always very dark here," she said.
I found a taxi in front of the building.
The taxi driver was friendly and helped me.
He asked about my new address.
I said my street number out loud.
"I know the street well," the driver said.
We drove towards the city.
I looked out of the window during the trip.
All the people wore warm coats and scarves.
Sara asked:
"Were you nervous?"
"Yes, a little," I answered.
But I also looked forward to my new apartment.
